\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {OPART MONTHLY PM
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Date_______________________      Engineer______________________________________________
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\par Center the 104mm phantom as precisely as possible (skew, levelness and position) in the head coil.  This will set you up to run 3 plane QAs, 3 plane FSEs to check eddy currents, and gradient gains.
\par 
\par Check the gradient offsets at the monitor jack on the front of the gradient amp.  Record the value of each channel and then adjust to zero.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par X  _________________mV\tab   Y_______________mV\tab \tab Z______________mV
\par 
\par 
\par Run the gradient gain settings.   Record the value of each channel then adjust to 99.4 +/-.2 if necessary.  Record the dial setting.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par X original gain number __________________    new(current) dial position __________________
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Y original gain number __________________    new(current) dial position __________________
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Z original gain number __________________    new(current) dial position __________________
\par 
\par Run Head1 & Head2 & Head3 and record the RF level, Center Frequency, Gain, Signal, Noise, & S/N
\par 
\par                 RF level           Gain                   CF                      Signal                        Noise                        S/N
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Head1   _________    __________     _______________     ___________          _________         _________
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Head2   _________    __________     _______________     ___________          _________         _________
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Head3   _________    __________     _______________     ___________          _________         _________
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Run the Head10, Head11 and Head12 FSE (change the FOV to 15
x15) sequences and check for shading or banding that might indicate an eddy current compensation problem.  Visually examine the image by using window width/level to see if there is any severe shading or banding.   Shading is measured by putting an ROI in 
t
he darkest area in the phantom and putting one in the lightest area and drawing an ROI that covers the entire image.  Check the numbers in the Statistics window and subtract the bright value from the darker value then divide that difference by the total i
mage ROI value.  
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Head11  _______________ %             Head12 _______________%            Head13 _______________%
\par 
\par Run the RF loopback test on the FSM/ADM and the TRM.________________. 
\par 
\par You should be testing the generator and bypasses to mak
e sure they are working correctly and returning to normal correctly.  Do a real world test, shut off the chiller and/or kill power to the system to make sure the bypasses and the generator are functioning properly.  
\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab _________________________________________
\par 
\par Also, check the fins on the chiller to make sure they are not clogged or soiled.____________
\par 
\par Inspect under the patient table inside the magnet to see if there might be any metal.______________
\par 
\par Do a site backup.____________
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {You should run \'93chkshim\'94 this will show magnet shim stability.________________
\par 
\par 
\par Check compressor pressures _________________________________________________________
\par 
\par 
\par Check Temperatures________________________________________________________________
\par 
\par 
\par Refer to Service Manual Chapter 14 for general site inspection details______________________
\par 
\par 
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {EVERY SIX MONTHS
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {You should check the TX coil tune and internal connections every six months._____________________
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par }}